  "id": "COMPOUND:12872 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Tenalisib is implicated in the regulation of CX-1 through a series of molecular interactions involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. These kinases are targets of multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, Javanicoside F, and Corticatic Acid E, all of which are known to interact with CX-1. The evidence suggests that Tenalisib acts as a common activator or modulator of these kinases, which in turn influence CX-1 through a shared biological pathway. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism where Tenalisib may exert its effects by activating or regulating these kinases, ultimately leading to a downstream effect on CX-1. The consistent presence of these targets across different compounds supports a role for Tenalisib in the modulation of CX-1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
